    "answer": {
      "short": "$MN\\parallel AC$ and $MN=\\frac12AC$.",
      "worked": "Let M and N be the midpoints of AB and BC. Then $\\frac{BM}{BA}=\\frac{BN}{BC}=\\frac{1}{2}$, and $\\angle MBN=\\angle ABC$ is common. Thus $\\triangle BMN\\sim\\triangle BAC$ by SAS. Corresponding angles give $\\angle BMN=\\angle BAC$, so $MN\\parallel AC$. Corresponding side ratios give $\\frac{MN}{AC}=\\frac{1}{2}$, hence $MN=\\frac{AC}{2}$.",
